たにありません。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "6d6b4ae49eea0f55695bdf7de604e8755990bbfe35bddb285187b9cc23750c44"}, {"item_id": "g.mixed-conditional", "sentence": "If I had studied medicine, I ____ a doctor now.", "options": ["would be", "would have been yesterday", "will been", "had be"], "answer": "would be", "hint_ja": "過去の仮定と現在の結果", "explanation_ja": "If + had + 過去分詞, would + 原形は、過去の事実が違っていたら現在はどうなっているかを表します。", "translation_ja": "医学を学んでいたら、今ごろ医師になっていたでしょう。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "2275ce3e104df1404ecb4d95933f65efbafd89a8be1d621da877b700f80ebcd3"}, {"item_id": "g.mixed-conditional", "sentence": "If she ____ the job offer last year, she would be living in London now.", "options": ["had accepted", "accepts", "will accept", "has accept"], "answer": "had accepted", "hint_ja": "過去の仮定と現在の結果", "explanation_ja": "If + had + 過去分詞, would + 原形は、過去の事実が違っていたら現在はどうなっているかを表します。", "translation_ja": "去年その内定を受けていたら、彼女は今ロンドンに住んでいるでしょう。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "29f567c9bee8e5b766491f70252ebdd9d462208a0b63cd8ee28f1d062d2351fd"}, {"item_id": "g.cleft", "sentence": "It was the noise ____ woke me up, not the light.", "options": ["that", "what", "where", "whose"], "answer": "that", "hint_ja": "特定の部分を強調する分裂文", "explanation_ja": "It is / was + 強調部分 + that ...。文の一部を取り出して焦点を当てます。", "translation_ja": "私を起こしたのは光ではなく、音でした。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "70b668624b3cac319b848a5956aff9006df4f257ea2adc335ca65230b53ee93d"}, {"item_id": "g.cleft", "sentence": "It was yesterday ____ she finally received the letter.", "options": ["that", "what", "whose", "where"], "answer": "that", "hint_ja": "特定の部分を強調する分裂文", "explanation_ja": "It is / was + 強調部分 + that ...。文の一部を取り出して焦点を当てます。", "translation_ja": "彼女がようやくその手紙を受け取ったのは昨日でした。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "5d1c8fdf76e6f22cf170a6798d97f6a7082804630ada7062b93b1cec277c9944"}, {"item_id": "g.modal-perfect", "sentence": "The lights are off and nobody answers. They must ____ home already.", "options": ["have gone", "had go", "has gone", "having go"], "answer": "have gone", "hint_ja": "過去への推量・後悔", "explanation_ja": "must have + 過去分詞は過去についての強い推量。should have + 過去分詞は、するべきだったのにしなかったことを表せます。", "translation_ja": "明かりは消え、返事もありません。彼らはもう帰宅したに違いありません。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "2691b16b52abc4fbae29e0f16c0a8e3639b6b4e509653e37850005d6813677f7"}, {"item_id": "g.modal-perfect", "sentence": "You should ____ me before changing the schedule.", "options": ["have told", "had tell", "has told", "having tell"], "answer": "have told", "hint_ja": "過去への推量・後悔", "explanation_ja": "must have + 過去分詞は過去についての強い推量。should have + 過去分詞は、するべきだったのにしなかったことを表せます。", "translation_ja": "予定を変える前に、私に知らせるべきでした。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "c196619e02d33b6d1525a89772c146498a40eb121b43d5524b7294853471aa63"}, {"item_id": "g.inverted-conditional", "sentence": "____ I known about the delay, I would have stayed at home.", "options": ["Had", "Have", "Did", "Would"], "answer": "Had", "hint_ja": "if を省略した仮定の倒置", "explanation_ja": "Had + 主語 + 過去分詞は If + 主語 + had + 過去分詞に相当します。形式的な文体で使われます。", "translation_ja": "遅延について知っていれば、家にいたのですが。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "ea4a7029357f1bbccd2ca50d9f8c501413c031f1392c754ecc31dc86336a86b8"}, {"item_id": "g.inverted-conditional", "sentence": "Had the team prepared more carefully, it ____ the error.", "options": ["would have avoided", "will avoid", "would avoided", "has avoiding"], "answer": "would have avoided", "hint_ja": "if を省略した仮定の倒置", "explanation_ja": "Had + 主語 + 過去分詞は If + 主語 + had + 過去分詞に相当します。形式的な文体で使われます。", "translation_ja": "チームがもっと慎重に準備していれば、そのミスを避けられたでしょう。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "238f5466fbe07af1bc72fdc08061c96724b524816ad746d3e0b4371363476548"}, {"item_id": "g.concessive-as", "sentence": "Tired ____ she was, she stayed to finish the work.", "options": ["as", "despite", "because of", "in spite of"], "answer": "as", "hint_ja": "形容詞を前に出す譲歩", "explanation_ja": "形容詞 + as + 主語 + 動詞で「〜だけれども」。Tired as she was は Although she was tired に相当します。", "translation_ja": "彼女は疲れていましたが、仕事を終えるために残りました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "519d4ff55732026d825b443b2dcb0759e6419e7fe2e68232b6c27a389329cbea"}, {"item_id": "g.concessive-as", "sentence": "Difficult ____ the task seemed, they decided to attempt it.", "options": ["as", "despite", "because of", "in spite of"], "answer": "as", "hint_ja": "形容詞を前に出す譲歩", "explanation_ja": "形容詞 + as + 主語 + 動詞で「〜だけれども」。Tired as she was は Although she was tired に相当します。", "translation_ja": "その課題は難しそうでしたが、彼らは挑戦することにしました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "631bded5c83c69a700f2a0a4267d0729d39f51ac7b43c3d3450360c03788f115"}, {"item_id": "g.not-until", "sentence": "Not until I reached home ____ that my wallet was missing.", "options": ["did I realise", "I did realise", "I realised", "realised did I"], "answer": "did I realise", "hint_ja": "「〜して初めて」の倒置", "explanation_ja": "Not until ... を文頭に置く場合、倒置するのは主節です。until 節の語順は通常のままです。", "translation_ja": "家に着いて初めて、財布がないことに気づきました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "3efbb6d1353c4a0414a882be0a5baa674179d161d0e247701412659d33f02bb0"}, {"item_id": "g.not-until", "sentence": "Not until the report was published ____ the full extent of the problem.", "options": ["did we understand", "we understood", "we did understand", "understood did we"], "answer": "did we understand", "hint_ja": "「〜して初めて」の倒置", "explanation_ja": "Not until ... を文頭に置く場合、倒置するのは主節です。until 節の語順は通常のままです。", "translation_ja": "報告書が公開されて初めて、私たちは問題の全容を理解しました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "02a0f385f6f8d1520beaae23b943efc806cefefbddda35d777613b8a553f5246"}, {"item_id": "g.perfect-participle", "sentence": "____ the report, she sent it to her manager.", "options": ["Having finished", "Having finish", "Have finishing", "Having been finish"], "answer": "Having finished", "hint_ja": "主節より前の動作を表す分詞構文", "explanation_ja": "Having + 過去分詞は、主節より先に完了した動作を示します。分詞構文と主節の意味上の主語は通常同じです。", "translation_ja": "報告書を書き終えてから、彼女はそれを上司に送りました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "76dce63eb3fc32f0e912d09728f9c8add48cf6289501e650bd36270512d546c4"}, {"item_id": "g.perfect-participle", "sentence": "____ all the options, we chose the least expensive one.", "options": ["Having considered", "Having consider", "Have considering", "Having been consider"], "answer": "Having considered", "hint_ja": "主節より前の動作を表す分詞構文", "explanation_ja": "Having + 過去分詞は、主節より先に完了した動作を示します。分詞構文と主節の意味上の主語は通常同じです。", "translation_ja": "すべての選択肢を検討したうえで、最も安いものを選びました。", "source": "Original Eego starter", "fingerprint": "8940dd6a24b074e01e49c9dab420c8371afd3b6b9a88fff4dbb9a6727aa06c99"}]}$eego$::jsonb;
BEGIN
  INSERT INTO eego.items(id,kind,level,label,meaning_ja,notes_ja,source,examples)
  SELECT x.id,x.kind,x.level,x.label,x.meaning_ja,x.notes_ja,x.source,x.examples
  FROM jsonb_to_recordset(d->'items') x(id text,kind text,level text,label text,meaning_ja text,notes_ja text,source text,examples jsonb)
  ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
  INSERT INTO eego.questions(item_id,sentence,options,answer,hint_ja,explanation_ja,translation_ja,source,fingerprint)
  SELECT x.item_id,x.sentence,x.options,x.answer,x.hint_ja,x.explanation_ja,x.translation_ja,x.source,x.fingerprint
  FROM jsonb_to_recordset(d->'questions') x(item_id text,sentence text,options jsonb,answer text,hint_ja text,explanation_ja text,translation_ja text,source text,fingerprint text)
  ON CONFLICT(fingerprint) DO NOTHING;
END $seed$;
